  "lines" : [
    {
      "fontSize" : 8,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        58.800000000000004,
        748.51210000000003,
        9.6000000000000014,
        9.3120000000000118
      ],
      "text" : "36"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 8,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        88.800000000000011,
        748.51210000000003,
        167.19999999999999,
        9.3120000000000118
      ],
      "text" : "The Fed Explained: What the Central Bank Does"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        692.64010000000007,
        409.69199999999978,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "counterparties. The IORB rate thus affects the federal funds rate and other short-term market"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        676.64010000000007,
        430.34299999999985,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "interest rates. (See box 3.3 for a discussion of how interest on reserve balances has proven to be"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        660.64010000000007,
        422.99599999999987,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "an effective tool for transmitting the FOMC’s target range for the federal funds rate to other inter-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        644.64010000000007,
        113.69799999999998,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "est rates in the economy.)"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        612.64010000000007,
        428.7439999999998,
        11.840000000000032
      ],
      "text" : "Open market operations. Over the years, the Federal Reserve has relied upon open market opera-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        596.64010000000007,
        431.69199999999967,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "tions as a tool of policy implementation. In conducting an open market operation, the Open Market"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        580.64010000000007,
        419.44499999999982,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "Desk at the Federal Reserve Bank of New York (or, the Desk) permanently or temporarily buys or"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        90,
        564.64010000000007,
        429.09399999999982,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "text" : "sells securities issued or guaranteed by the U.S. Treasury or U.S. government agencies. When the"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 14,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        102.5,
        517.49610000000007,
        346.77440000000001,
        16.576000000000022
      ],
      "text" : "Box 3.3. Interest on Reserve Balances as a Key Tool of"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 14,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        103.494,
        501.49410000000006,
        203.90860000000001,
        16.575999999999965
      ],
      "text" : "Monetary Policy Implementation"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 9,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        102.5,
        478.54610000000002,
        406.43639999999976,
        10.656000000000006
      ],
      "text" : "The Federal Reserve uses interest on reserve balances as a key tool to anchor the federal funds rate"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 9,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        103.499,
        467.54810000000003,
        390.14729999999986,
        10.656000000000006
      ],
      "text" : "in the target range. The interest on reserve balances (IORB) rate acts as a benchmark for banks"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 9,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        103.499,
        456.55010000000004,
        287.59410000000003,
        10.656000000000006
      ],
      "text" : "when determining the interest rate to charge in their lending activities."
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 9,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        102.5,
        433.54610000000002,
        401.89319999999981,
        10.475999999999999
      ],
      "text" : "In particular, banks should require a rate in lending to households and businesses and others at least"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 9,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        103.499,
        422.54810000000003,
        401.34959999999967,
        10.475999999999999
      ],
      "text" : "as high as they can earn on balances maintained in their reserve accounts at the Federal Reserve. As"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 9,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        103.499,
        411.55010000000004,
        402.52139999999974,
        10.475999999999999
      ],
      "text" : "a result, the setting of the IORB rate affects borrowing and lending in overnight money markets as well"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 9,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        103.499,
        400.55210000000005,
        158.39730000000006,
        10.475999999999999
      ],
      "text" : "as influences broader financial markets."
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 9,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        102.5,
        383.55110000000008,
        398.15549999999973,
        10.475999999999999
      ],
      "text" : "When the FOMC increased the target range for the federal funds rate between late 2015 and the end"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 9,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        103.499,
        372.55310000000009,
        395.23319999999978,
        10.475999999999999
      ],
      "text" : "of 2018, there was a corresponding change to the interest on required and excess reserves rates to"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 9,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        103.499,
        361.5551000000001,
        386.18459999999993,
        10.475999999999999
      ],
      "text" : "move the federal funds rate into the target range. Other overnight money market rates also moved"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 9,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        103.499,
        350.5571000000001,
        397.75049999999987,
        10.475999999999999
      ],
      "text" : "up (figure A). Rates in short-term funding markets—such as commercial paper rates and Treasury bill"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 9,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        103.499,
        339.55910000000011,
        393.61049999999989,
        10.475999999999999
      ],
      "text" : "rates—moved higher as well (figure B). In 2019 and 2020, when the FOMC lowered the target range"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 9,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        103.499,
        328.56110000000012,
        380.69639999999981,
        10.475999999999999
      ],
      "text" : "for the federal funds rate, the Federal Reserve lowered the interest rates on required and excess"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 9,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        103.499,
        317.56310000000013,
        397.03229999999974,
        10.475999999999999
      ],
      "text" : "reserves and short-term rates declined. These increases and decreases in the general level of short-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 9,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        103.499,
        306.56510000000014,
        384.74549999999977,
        10.475999999999999
      ],
      "text" : "term rates, together with the expected future path of short-term rates, then influenced the level of"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 9,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        103.499,
        295.56710000000015,
        295.87229999999977,
        10.475999999999999
      ],
      "text" : "other financial asset prices and overall financial conditions in the economy."
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 8,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        102.58000000000001,
        271.45680000000004,
        85.463999999999999,
        9.0480000000000018
      ],
      "text" : "A. Overnight money market rates"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 6,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        103.6576,
        124.9385,
        160.64999999999998,
        6.7620000000000005
